---

<section id="how-it-works" class="py-12 md:py-16 lg:py-20 border-y border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--surface-tint)]">
  <div class="site-container">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-14 items-center">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Story Headline & CTA (lg:col-span-5) -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 flex flex-col justify-center">
        <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-[var(--brand)] mb-3">
          HOW IT ALL STARTED
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.6rem] font-extrabold text-[var(--ink)] tracking-tight leading-[1.15] mb-6">
          I thought I understood databases.
          <span class="text-[var(--brand)]">There was one way to find out.</span>
        </h2>

        <!-- Read how that went button -->
        <div>
          <a
            href="https://lokesh.me/building-columnar-analytics-database-python"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-white hover:bg-[var(--lavender)] text-xs font-bold text-[var(--ink)] hover:text-[var(--brand)] hover:border-[var(--brand)]/30 transition-all shadow-xs"
          >
            <span>Read how that went</span>
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-[var(--brand)]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: 3-Step Process Flow (lg:col-span-7) -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 sm:gap-8">
          
          <!-- Step 1: The confidence -->
          <div class="flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3.5">
              <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] text-white font-mono font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs">
                1
              </div>
              <!-- Connecting arrow pointing right to step 2 (visible on md+) -->
              <div class="hidden md:block text-[var(--brand)]/40 text-base select-none font-bold pr-2">
                →
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-2">
              The confidence
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
              After years of operating, tuning, and optimising analytical engines, I thought I understood the machinery pretty well.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 2: The itch -->
          <div class="flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3.5">
              <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] text-white font-mono font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs">
                2
              </div>
              <!-- Connecting arrow pointing right to step 3 (visible on md+) -->
              <div class="hidden md:block text-[var(--brand)]/40 text-base select-none font-bold pr-2">
                →
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-2">
              The itch
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
              But I still wanted to follow one query all the way down &mdash; to see which bytes moved, which values were decoded, and where the time actually went.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 3: The questionable decision -->
          <div class="flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3.5">
              <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] text-white font-mono font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs">
                3
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-2">
              The questionable decision
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
              So I built a columnar database in Python.
            </p>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--muted)]/80 italic leading-relaxed mt-2">
              It seemed reasonable at the time.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
